# ticket-folder-missing — the current user has no folder in the Spike Board space:
# the Confluence handover (Template G) must tell them to create one, with a location.
# The prompt pre-answers every interview step so a single headless turn can reach the ticket.
NEEDS=no-folder
IFS= read -r -d '' PROMPT <<'PROMPT_EOF' || true
Use the spike-board:spike-ticket skill. A parallel topic that leaves my chain alone: Terraform. I've never used it. To save round-trips, here are my answers to everything you'll ask: I can't answer any of the exit questions confidently — none of them. I have used every prerequisite for real. Go all the way to the finished ticket, filing instructions, and queue in this one reply.
PROMPT_EOF
IFS= read -r -d '' MUST <<'MUST_EOF' || true
\*\*Confluence\*\*
- Space: Spike Board
- Folder: you don't have one yet
create a folder \(not a page\) at the top level of the space
\*\*Filing\*\*
- Project: SCRUM
MUST_EOF
IFS= read -r -d '' MUST_NOT <<'MUST_NOT_EOF' || true
in your folder in the Spike Board space
Isaiah|Austin|Andrew
⟨|⟩
MUST_NOT_EOF
